112	      }
113	      // `trigger` says whether the scheduler asks this task at every tick, and is
114	      // OPTIONAL for one convergence window (#1789) — absent, the door reads it off
115	      // the shape of the conditions, and `legacy-task-fields` is what says so. What
116	      // is checked here is a STATED one: the value, and the one pairing that cannot
117	      // work. A `schedule` task whose expression reads the ITEM has nothing to be
118	      // judged against at a tick — the scheduler's own ask carries no item — so the
119	      // term errors on every tick and the task's lane fills with failed runs rather
120	      // than ever declining.
121	      if (decl.has('trigger')) {
